grammar Ll1AltPrefixConflict

// X's two alternatives are the literals "a" and "aa", disjoint as identities but
// "a" is a prefix of "aa". S calls X twice, so on input `aa` the longest-match
// dispatch takes X = "aa" for the first call and the second X then fails at
// end of input. The only valid parse is X = "a" twice. A sound classifier routes
// X through GLL.
S = X X
X = "a" | "aa"
